WEBVTT

1
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:58.000
Anna H.: Saturday, 09:10 to 09:52. One clinic chain's integration retried in a loop and exhausted the global API rate limit. 212 clinics saw booking errors for 42 minutes; no data was lost.

2
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:13.000
Anna H.: Shah from support says 31 clinics wrote in during the outage, and every ticket was answered within the hour.

3
00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:12.000
Chidi O.: Root cause: limits are global, not per clinic, so one noisy client affects everyone. And the 429 alert only fired on the hourly rollup.

4
00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:39.000
Chidi O.: Rate limits become per clinic, with the global one as a backstop: per-clinic limits, this week, nothing else goes in first.

5
00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:11.000
Anna H.: Agreed: the per-clinic limit ships before any new API feature.

6
00:26:15.000 --> 00:26:23.000
Chidi O.: On alerting, we need a five-minute alert, not the hourly one: 429s above 1% for five minutes.

7
00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:07.000
Anna H.: A monitoring gap turned a five-minute problem into a 42-minute outage.

8
00:33:40.000 --> 00:33:47.000
Anna H.: Shah can help with the wording. I'll write the note to the affected clinics today.

9
00:37:20.000 --> 00:37:30.000
Chidi O.: Should the noisy chain get a dedicated limit, or should we ask them to fix their retries? We're waiting on their engineering contact.
